From: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:23:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Don't pause on DOM breakpoints during document
 lifecycle updates

FlyWeb next batch: from branch-heads/8078 dabab2fd13. Applied after seguridad/siguiente/chromium/0005; applies cleanly (identical diff). No brave-core patches or chromium_src for these files.

Original change's description:
> Don't pause on DOM breakpoints during document lifecycle updates
>
> DOM breakpoints could fire for DOM mutations that happen inside a
> lifecycle update, such as the disposal of pseudo-elements during style
> recalc. Pausing there runs a nested message loop in which the debugger
> client can run arbitrary script (e.g. via Runtime.evaluate), which the
> style recalc code is not prepared for. For example, calling
> ViewTransition.skipTransition() while paused in the removal of a
> ::view-transition-image-pair frees the list of view transition names
> that Element::UpdateTransitionPseudoElements() is iterating, causing a
> use-after-free on resume.
>
> Such mutations are not caused by script, so skip the pause when the
> document lifecycle doesn't allow tree mutations. Script-initiated
> mutations still pause as before.
>
